speaker: Brandon Warren
---
bio:

Brandon Warren has worked as a software engineer for over 20 years, 12 of those years with Python as his language of choice. He is currently working at Zonar Systems, building cloud-based telematics applications. He is not a physicist, but that’s the point of his talk - non-scientists can have fun learning about the quantum world, too.
---
title: Introduction to the Quantum Bit
---
abstract:
In this talk, I’ll introduce the quantum bit, or qubit, and talk about two special properties of quantum bits: quantum superposition and quantum entanglement. We’ll run quantum circuits on a laptop and on a real quantum computer.

Python familiarity would be helpful, but is not required.
